From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000005 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton <fourth@devpins.org>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium: self-power USB host VBUS

Patch 0002 pins &usb_1_dwc3 to dr_mode = "host", but that alone leaves the
USB-C port electrically dead: dwc3-qcom only asserts the UTMI_OTG_VBUS_VALID
*signal* and never drives 5 V, and mainline has no PMI8998 OTG-boost
regulator. A self-powered USB device (Chord Mojo 2) only asserts its D+
pull-up once it sees real VBUS, so with a plain passive OTG cable nothing
enumerated unless 5 V was fed onto the bus from outside the phone (a powered
Y-cable, or the Mojo's own power-output mode). The downstream Android kernel
"just works" because its qpnp-smb2 driver turns on the PMI8998 OTG boost.

Add the PMI8998 USB VBUS boost regulator at the DCDC peripheral base 0x1100
(under pmi8998_lsid0, the same SPMI LSID as the disabled charger@1000, bound
independently). It is driven by the qcom,pmi8998-vbus-reg support added in
patch 0004 and needs CONFIG_REGULATOR_QCOM_USB_VBUS=y.

beryllium has no working Type-C role switch / usb-connector graph, so there
is no consumer to enable VBUS on demand; mark the regulator regulator-always-on
(+boot-on) so it comes up at boot and is not torn down by regulator_init_complete
as an unused supply. This mirrors the accepted db845c approach for host VBUS
without a connector node.

The override appends to the shared -common.dtsi after the audio-disable block
from patch 0003, so it covers both the EBBG and Tianma panel variants; it
locates by the trailing &slimbam override, so the line number is approximate
and patch(1) resolves it by offset.

Warning: with the phone now sourcing VBUS, do NOT also enable the Mojo 2's own
power-output/charging mode -- two 5 V sources must not fight on the bus.

Signed-off-by: Anton <fourth@devpins.org>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm845-xiaomi-beryllium-common.dtsi
@@ -941,4 +941,20 @@
 &sound { status = "disabled"; };
 &wcd9340 { status = "disabled"; };
 &slim { status = "disabled"; };
 &slimbam { status = "disabled"; };
+
+/* Self-power USB VBUS in permanent host mode (PMI8998 OTG boost). Needs the
+ * qcom,pmi8998-vbus-reg driver (patch 0004) + CONFIG_REGULATOR_QCOM_USB_VBUS=y.
+ * No role-switch/connector on beryllium -> always-on (db845c precedent), else
+ * the regulator core disables it as unused. Don't also enable the Mojo 2's own
+ * power output -- avoid dual-sourcing VBUS. */
+&pmi8998_lsid0 {
+	pmi8998_vbus: usb-vbus-regulator@1100 {
+		compatible = "qcom,pmi8998-vbus-reg";
+		reg = <0x1100>;
+		regulator-min-microamp = <500000>;
+		regulator-max-microamp = <1000000>;
+		regulator-always-on;
+		regulator-boot-on;
+	};
+};
